  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given word &#39;VOWELS&#39;</p><p>Number of words Arranging all the letters&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>!</mo></math></p><p>In the given word Consonants are W, L, S.</p><p>Treating all the consonants as one unit then number of units will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>No of such arrangements&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>VOWELS&nbsp;all the consonants never come together <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math>Total - all consonants come together <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>576</mn></math></p>",
